  "summary": "The Kane County Board approved renewing the Kane County Sheriff's Office contract with Flock Safety for 25 license plate reader cameras at $72,000 annually. Undersheriff Amy Johnson said the cameras help significantly and that the office would ideally expand to 45-50 cameras. The renewal comes as nearby Illinois communities like Oak Park and Evanston have ended Flock contracts over immigration data-sharing concerns.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "the Kane County Board approved a renewal of the Kane County Sheriff's Office's contract with Flock Safety for its license plate reader cameras throughout the county",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "both Oak Park and Evanston halted their contracts with Flock amid concern over information possibly being shared with federal immigration agencies",
      "paragraph_idx": 8
    },
    {
      "quote": "The contract renewal comes at a cost of $72,000 annually",
      "paragraph_idx": 11
    }
  ],
